<title>USA: Millennium America may issue $750 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Millennium America may issue $750 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Millennium America Inc is expected to issue $750 million in a two-tranche deal, said lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co on Thursday.</p>
<p>The first tranche is expected to consist of $500 million in 10-year senior notes, with price talk of 85 to 88 basis points.</p>
<p>The second tranche is expected to consist of $250 million in 30-year senior debentures, with price talk in the range of 115 to 118 basis points.</p>
<p>Both issues are non-callable and are rated Baa3/BBB-minus.</p>
<p>- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678</p>
</text>
